  "question": {
    "text": "An electron of mass <math><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;has de-Broglie wavelength <math><msup><mrow><mi>&nbsp;</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;when accelerated through potential difference <math><msup><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup></math>. When proton of mass <math><msup><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></math>, is accelerated through potential difference <math><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup></math>, the de-Broglie wavelength associated with it will be (Assume that wavelength is determined at low voltage)",
